Stripe, LLC. is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone's reach while doing the most important work of your career.

What you’ll do

Responsibilities

• Working with teams across the organization to understand pain points in their infrastructure usage to find common ideas and work to create solutions which span multiple domains;

• Define and produce high quality written proposals, communications and documentation.&nbsp;

• Execute on technical programs that require deep systems and engineering level knowledge;

• Partner with Engineering Managers, Tech Leads, Engineers and other Technical Program Managers to define, scope and drive large programs to conclusion;&nbsp;

• Play a key part in shaping the technical design, predicting technical roadblocks by collaborating with engineers, and identifying trade-offs;

• Develop, implement, and iterate on program management techniques, frameworks, and KPIs to achieve goals with well defined success criteria;

• Elevate the execution muscle of engineering teams around you;

• Train them to be better at delivery where needed;

• Help influence peers / stakeholders and build consensus while dealing with ambiguity;

• Leverage data and acquired knowledge to drive strategic decisions at an engineering leadership level;

• Create widely circulated plans, driving consistency, clarity and building alignment across teams;

• Operationalize and execute critical cross functional programs spanning multiple engineering organizations for Infrastructure (Developer Infrastructure, Core Infrastructure, Service Infrastructure);

• Shape technical design, predicting technical roadblocks by collaborating with engineers, and identify trade-offs;

• Drive programs that span across Stripe in the core infrastructure of Stripe’s payment systems;

• Responsible for the successful definition, cross-functional strategy, planning and execution of large-scale technical programs.&nbsp;

• Solve complex problems and enable products and infrastructure at scale;

• Deliver exceptional results through building and implementing solutions that scale while protecting our users and serving the business; and

• Demonstrate deep technical expertise in software infrastructure (e.g. AWS Cloud Infrastructure, Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud, Oracle Cloud, etc.)

Who you are

Minimum requirements

• Must have a Bachelor's degree or foreign equivalent in Engineering, Computer Science, Management Information Systems, or a related field, plus 5 years of progressive, postbaccalaureate experience in Software engineering, systems engineering or technical program management.

• 4 years experience in Core infrastructure including database, cloud compute, networking and services;

